config.stackupup.compat.inventoryExpansion.name=Inventory Capacity Expansion
config.stackupup.compat.inventoryExpansion.name.tooltip=Inventory capacity expansion is enabled by default for new or missing configuration (broad-default); an existing explicit false remains off, and setting false is a restart-time emergency fallback. Listed modIds selectively bypass capacity expansion; unlisted inventories remain eligible. ItemStack and other non-capacity behavior remain independent. Changes require a restart.
config.stackupup.compat.inventoryExpansion.enabled.name=Enable Inventory Capacity Expansion
config.stackupup.general.enableDslRules.tooltip=Load DSL v2 rules from config/stackupup/*.su, with world and user overrides layered on top.
config.stackupup.compat.inventoryExpansion.enabled.tooltip=Enable generic third-party inventory and optional late capacity expansion. New or missing configuration defaults to broad expansion; an existing explicit false remains off, and setting false is a restart-time emergency fallback. Vanilla player/chest/container stack-rule support remains active. Changes require restart.
config.stackupup.client.tooltipStackDisplayMode.tooltip=Choose when to show current stack size and max stack size in tooltips.
config.stackupup.general.ruleComplexityWarnings.tooltip=Warn when the ruleset becomes unusually large or long.
config.stackupup.compat.vanilla.craftingSlotLimit.tooltip=Crafting container slot limit. Mainly a Performance setting rather than a balance setting: holding Shift to batch-craft very large stacks can cause severe lag. Values above 0 set a custom limit; 0 keeps vanilla behavior.
config.stackupup.compat.nuclearcraft.speedUpgradeLimit.tooltip=Speed upgrade stack limit. Values above 0 set a custom limit; 0 keeps NuclearCraft's native behavior.
config.stackupup.compat.nuclearcraft.energyUpgradeLimit.tooltip=Energy upgrade stack limit. Values above 0 set a custom limit; 0 keeps NuclearCraft's native behavior.
config.stackupup.compat.inventoryStackLimitBlacklist.modIds.tooltip=Select Forge mod IDs whose attributable owned-package inventories bypass capacity expansion and whose capacity mixins are skipped; an empty list is a no-op and does not change existing expansion behavior. Unlisted mods remain eligible when enabled. Shared ownerless objects, optional inherited constructors and private delegates remain UNKNOWN. Review unsafe containers and restart after changes; this does not prove third-party compatibility.

