commands.stackupup.inspect.no_target=No loaded inventory/capability target at this location.
commands.stackupup.inspect.slot_range=Slot %s is outside the target's %s slots (zero-based).
commands.stackupup.inspect.header=Read-only inspection: %s selected slots; object IDs are local to this report.
commands.stackupup.inspect.object=Object #%s %s: %s; Forge owned-package modId candidates: %s
commands.stackupup.inspect.slot=Slot %s -> backing index %s; Slot object #%s; receiver #%s
commands.stackupup.inspect.delegate_unknown=Delegate: UNKNOWN where no supported public accessor exists; no reflection or write probe performed.
commands.stackupup.inspect.truncated=Omitted %s slots; use inspect slot N (or block ... slot N) to focus on another slot.
commands.stackupup.inspect.config=Review candidate for %s in config/stackupup.cfg (not applied): %s
commands.stackupup.inspect.warning=Candidates are not a capacity/conservation proof. Class names are diagnostic only; no class-name setting exists. Empty blacklist is a no-op; listed mod IDs exclude attributable receiver classes or supported public owners, not ItemStack rules. Inheriting a listed superclass or implementing a listed interface alone does not exclude an unlisted addon. Shared creator ownership, private delegates and optional receiverless constructor paths remain UNKNOWN; do not assume they are excluded or safe. Review entries and restart.
